<%# Wrapper for the complete ticket display with separate frames for header and content %>
<%# data-assistant-context (S4 T2 step 5b, plan §7.3): the page NAMES the object it
    is showing, so the assistant panel can offer to take it over without anybody
    clicking. Deliberately not the Stimulus value the button next door uses -- a
    click has a receiver that reads its own controller, this has none: the panel
    has to SEARCH the page for it after a navigation (Rev. 13 reserved the name
    for exactly this).

    Written by AssistantContextHelper, not by hand here, because this wrapper is
    not the only root #ticket_display_frame can hold: a generated summary fills
    the same frame with _ticket_content_for_frame instead, which is why THAT
    partial asks the same helper. The value, the bound and the gate have one
    owner; the two call sites are the frame's two roots, not two copies of a rule.

    ⚠️ The previous version counted the render sites in this comment and was
    wrong twice: it said six, listed seven, and there are eight. The count was
    never the point -- the frame having more than one root is. %>
<div data-controller="timeline-filter" data-ticket-id="<%= ticket.id %>"
     <%= assistant_context_attributes(ticket) %>>
  <%# Open for 5 seconds = read: every unread notification of the viewer about this
      ticket (Notifications::MarkTicketRead, user decision 30.09.2026), the same rule
      and controller as the inbox pane. The pane passes mark_notifications_read: false,
      it runs its own timer on the selected notification. %>
  <% if local_assigns.fetch(:mark_notifications_read, true) &&
        current_user.notifications.channel_in_app.unread.exists?(notifiable: ticket) %>
    <div hidden data-controller="pane-mark-read-delay"
         data-pane-mark-read-delay-url-value="<%= organisation_project_ticket_notification_read_path(ticket.organisation_id, ticket.project_id, ticket) %>"></div>
  <% end %>
  <%# Header in a container with consistent spacing %>
  <div class="header-compact">
    <%= render 'organisations/tickets/ticket_header_show',
               ticket: ticket,
               frame_id: 'ticket-header-content',
               project: defined?(project) ? project : @project,
               current_organisation: defined?(current_organisation) ? current_organisation : @current_organisation %>
  </div>

  <%# Content without header (timeline loads lazily via turbo-frame) %>
  <%= render 'organisations/tickets/ticket_content_for_frame',
             ticket: ticket,
             post: post,
             project: project,
             current_organisation: current_organisation %>
</div>
